# Vercel project with Root Directory `amd/mcp` (README "Deploy on Vercel"). Keeps secrets and dev files out of
# CLI uploads (git deploys never contain them: they are git-ignored). A denylist, not a `/*` allowlist, so it means
# the same whether Vercel anchors it at amd/mcp or at the repo root. vercel.json `excludeFiles` also keeps tests
# and tooling out of the function bundle.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
tests
client_example.py
